Apple camera: keep the format that was chosen.

SDL picks an AVCaptureDeviceFormat matching the spec the application asked
for and assigns it to the device's activeFormat. Twenty lines later it sets
the session's preset to AVCaptureSessionPresetHigh, and Apple's headers say
those two are mutually exclusive:

    On iOS, use of AVCaptureDevice's setActiveFormat: and AVCaptureSession's
    setSessionPreset: are mutually exclusive. If you set the AVCaptureSession's
    sessionPreset property, the session assumes control of its input devices,
    and configures their activeFormat appropriately.

So the chosen format is discarded and the device runs at whatever the preset
means, which on an iPhone is 1920x1080. The size is then asked for again
through AVCaptureVideoDataOutput's videoSettings, where the width and height
keys are not reliably honoured and where the source's aspect ratio wins when
they are. The frames that arrive are a different shape and size than the spec
SDL believes it negotiated, and SDL goes on to convert each one using the
size it expected rather than the size that came: too small and the
destination keeps its zeroed remainder, too wide and each row runs into the
next. Neither the conversion's result nor SDL_StretchSurface's is checked.

Two changes, both in SDL_camera_coremedia.m:

  - Ask for AVCaptureSessionPresetInputPriority, which is the documented way
    to say "leave my device's format alone".
  - Set activeFormat again after the input has been added, inside the same
    lockForConfiguration that already re-applies the frame duration. Adding
    an input is where the session reconfigures the device, which is why the
    frame rate is already set twice in this function; the format needs the
    same treatment and was missed. It goes first because setting a format
    resets the frame duration to that format's default.

Applies to SDL3-3.4.16. Both preset constants are old enough for the floors
this project builds against (iOS 14, macOS 11). Drop this file when the fix
is upstream.

--- a/src/camera/coremedia/SDL_camera_coremedia.m
+++ b/src/camera/coremedia/SDL_camera_coremedia.m
@@ -388,7 +388,11 @@
         return SDL_SetError("Failed to allocate/init AVCaptureSession");
     }
 
-    session.sessionPreset = AVCaptureSessionPresetHigh;
+    // Input priority, so the session leaves the device's activeFormat
+    // alone. Any other preset makes the session take charge of its
+    // inputs and reconfigure them, throwing away the format chosen
+    // above.
+    session.sessionPreset = AVCaptureSessionPresetInputPriority;
 #if defined(SDL_PLATFORM_IOS)
     if (@available(iOS 10.0, tvOS 17.0, *)) {
         session.automaticallyConfiguresCaptureDeviceForWideColor = NO;
@@ -436,9 +440,14 @@
     }
     [session addOutput:output];
 
-    // Try to set the frame rate on the device (preferred modern approach)
+    // Set the format and the frame rate on the device (preferred modern
+    // approach). Again, and after the input has been added: adding an input
+    // is where the session reconfigures the device, so anything set before
+    // that is gone by now. The format goes first because setting it resets
+    // the frame duration to that format's default.
     if ([avdevice lockForConfiguration:nil]) {
         @try {
+            avdevice.activeFormat = spec_format;
